  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Guidehouse has $473M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 276 awards with an average award size of $1.7M. Obligations are down 10.7% year over year. Guidehouse saw a multi-year revenue climb from $28.2M in FY21 to a peak of $747M in FY24, before falling to $530M in FY25 and then to $473M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $134M obligated so far, followed by the Department of the Interior with $85.2M and the Department of Homeland Security with $54M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the largest NAICS market with $205M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services with $108M and Other Accounting Services with $94.6M. Current-year totals are partial, representing fiscal year to date activity rather than full-year results. This snapshot highlights where Guidehouse concentrates federal work by agency and market, and how current obligations compare with recent fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Guidehouse's largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is Guidehouse's largest federal customer with $134M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior follows with $85.2M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $54M. The Department of Health and Human Services and the Department of Justice each obligated $51M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets account for Guidehouse's federal work?",
        "body": "Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the largest market with $205M in obligations. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Accounting Services are the next largest markets with $108M and $94.6M respectively. Custom Computer Programming Services and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services add $25M and $16.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Guidehouse make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Guidehouse has $473M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Guidehouse recorded 276 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $1.7M, and obligations are down 10.7% year over year. Guidehouse's obligations rose from $28.2M in FY21 to $747M in FY24 before falling to $530M in FY25 and $473M in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Guidehouse?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, the Department of the Interior, and the Department of Homeland Security are Guidehouse's top buyers in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $134M, the Department of the Interior obligated $85.2M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $54M. Other buying agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services and the Department of Justice at $51M each."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Guidehouse sell to the government?",
      "a": "Guidehouse primarily sells management consulting, IT, and accounting services to the government. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services account for $205M, Computer Systems Design Services account for $108M, and Other Accounting Services account for $94.6M in FY2026 to date. Guidehouse also delivers Custom Computer Programming Services and other professional and technical services."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which Guidehouse contracts are expiring soon?",
